---
import Content from '../../layouts/Content.astro';
import { site } from '../../config';
import { careGroups, careSvgAttrs } from '../../lib/careSymbols';

const article = {
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Laundry care symbols explained',
  author: { '@id': `${site.url}/#business` },
  publisher: { '@id': `${site.url}/#business` },
  mainEntityOfPage: `${site.url}/guides/care-labels/`,
  inLanguage: 'en-IN',
};
---

<Content
  title="Laundry care symbols explained: washing, drying and ironing labels | dhobermans"
  description="What the symbols on your clothing care label mean: washing temperatures, bleaching, tumble drying, ironing and dry cleaning, explained in plain language."
  h1="Care label guide"
  lead="What the symbols on your clothing label mean, in plain language."
  schema={[article]}
  flow="question"
  cta="Send us a photo of the label"
>
  <h2>How to read a care label</h2>
  <p>
    Care labels use five families of symbols, usually in this order: washing (a tub), bleaching (a triangle), drying (a square), ironing (an
    iron) and professional cleaning (a circle). A cross through any symbol means do not. Dots show heat: more dots, more heat.
  </p>

  {
    careGroups.map((g) => (
      <>
        <h2>{g.name}</h2>
        <ul class="symbols">
          {g.symbols.map((sym) => (
            <li>
              <span class="symbols__art" set:html={`<svg ${careSvgAttrs}>${sym.svg}</svg>`} />
              <span>
                <strong>{sym.title}</strong>
                {sym.text}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </>
    ))
  }

  <h2>Still unsure?</h2>
  <p class="note">
    Symbols follow the international care-labelling standard (ISO 3758). Some labels use slightly different drawings. Send us a photo of the
    label and we will tell you how the item should be cleaned. For stains, see the <a href="/guides/stain-removal/">stain removal guide</a>; for
    garments marked with a circle, see <a href="/services/dry-cleaning/">dry cleaning</a>.
  </p>
</Content>

<style>
  .symbols {
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 0 !important;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .symbols li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 56px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .symbols__art {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .symbols__art :global(svg) {
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
  }

  .symbols strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
